          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In general, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categories"} categories
            (or, more generally, any category-like things, such as
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/objects"} objects
            of some
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-category"} 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+structure"} algebraic structure
            %em lax morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
            is one which “preserves” the algebraic structure only up to a not-necessarily invertible transformation.
          %p
            Of course, this transformation goes in one particular direction; a
            %em colax morphism
            is one where the transformation goes in the other direction. The case of 2-monads, below, provides an almost universally applicable way to decide which direction is “lax” and which is “colax”.
          %h2#definition Definition
          %h3#for_algebras_of_2monads For algebras of 2-monads
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-monad"} 2-monad
            on a 2-category
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            be (strict, pseudo, or even lax or colax)
            = succeed "-algebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %strong
              lax
              = succeed "-morphism" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi A
                  %mo →
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon A\to B
            is a morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            together with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-cell"} 2-cell
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi T
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %mi B
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi a
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi b
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi A
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ T A &amp; \overset{T f}{\to} &amp; T B\\
                  ^{a} \downarrow &amp; \swArrow &amp; \downarrow^{b}\\
                  A &amp; \underset{f}{\to} &amp; B}
          %p satisfying some axioms.
          %p
            If the 2-cell goes in the other direction, then we say
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a
            %strong
              colax
              = succeed "-morphism" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            (or
            = succeed ")." do
              %strong
                oplax
                = succeed "-morphism" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphism" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphism," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi co
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{co}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mi co
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^{co}
            is the induced 2-monad on the 2-cell dual
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi K
                    %mi co
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{co}
            (see
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/opposite+2-category"} opposite 2-category
          %p
            If the 2-cell is invertible, we call
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            a
            %strong pseudo
            or
            %strong strong
            = succeed "-morphism." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %h3#for_coalgebras_of_2comonads For coalgebras of 2-comonads
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            be a 2-comonad on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi K
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi C
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
            be
            = succeed "-coalgebras." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %strong
              lax
              = succeed "-morphism" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi C
                  %mo →
                  %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f\colon C\to D
            is a morphism in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            together with a 2-cell
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %mover
                            %mo →
                            %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi D
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo
                            %mi c
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                          %mo ⇙
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                            %mi d
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mi C
                        %mtd
                          %munder
                            %mo →
                            %mrow
                              %mi W
                              %mi f
                        %mtd
                          %mi W
                          %mi D
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ C &amp; \overset{f}{\to} &amp; D\\
                  ^{c} \downarrow &amp; \swArrow &amp; \downarrow^{d}\\
                  W C &amp; \underset{W f}{\to} &amp; W D}
          %p satisfying some axioms.
          %p
            Note that a lax morphism of algebras for the 2-comonad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is a
            %em colax
            morphism of algebras for the 2-monad
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W^{op}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is a 2-monad with a right
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi T
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*
            automatically becomes a 2-comonad such that
            = succeed "-coalgebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*
            = succeed "-algebras," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphisms." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T^*
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+monoidal+functor"} lax monoidal functor
                is a lax morphism for the 2-monad on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cat"} Cat
                whose algebras are
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+categories"} monoidal categories
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/oplax+monoidal+functor"} oplax monoidal functor
                is a colax morphism for this 2-monad.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+natural+transformation"} lax natural transformation
                between
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-functors"} 2-functors
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                      %mo →
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C\to D
                is a lax morphism for the 2-monad on
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi ob
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi C
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mi D
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} [ob(C),D]
                whose algebras are 2-functors (which exists if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is cocomplete and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi C
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C
                is small). Similarly, an oplax natural transformation is a colax morphism for this 2-monad. If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
                is also complete, then this 2-monad has a right adjoint, which then as usual becomes a 2-comonad whose coalgebras are also 2-functors. The above conventions for lax morphisms between coalgebras mean that a lax natural transformation is unambiguously “lax” rather than “colax”, whether we regard the 2-functors as algebras for a 2-monad or coalgebras for a 2-comonad.
              %p Some authors have tried to change the traditional meanings of “lax” and “colax” in this case, but the general framework of 2-monads gives a good argument for keeping it this way (even if in this particular case, oplax transformations are more common or useful).
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+functor"} lax functor
                between 2-categories is a lax morphism for the 2-monad on Cat-graphs whose algebras are 2-categories.
            %li
              %p
                A
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax+algebra+for+a+2-monad"} lax algebra for a 2-monad
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is a lax morphism
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mo →
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T\to \langle A,A\rangle
                for the 2-monad whose algebras are 2-monads, where
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                      %mi A
                      %mo ,
                      %mi A
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle A,A\rangle
                is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/codensity+monad"} codensity monad
                of the object
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi A
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %li
              %p
                If
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                is a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lax-idempotent+2-monad"} lax-idempotent 2-monad
                %em every
                morphism in the underlying 2-category
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                between (the objects underlying)
                = succeed "-algebras" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                = succeed "-morphism." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi T
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimits"} colimits
                is a lax morphism for the 2-monad which assigns those colimits; the unique lax structure map is the canonical comparison
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi colim
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi F
                        %mo ∘
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo →
                        %mi F
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi colim
                        %mi D
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} colim (F\circ D) \to F(colim D)
            %li
              %p
                For
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/probability+monads"} probability monads
                on a
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+posetal+2-category"} locally posetal 2-category
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Radon+monad#the_ordered_case"} ordered Radon monad
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/concave+maps"} concave maps
                or a suitable generalization thereof.
          %h2#categories_of_lax_morphisms Categories of lax morphisms
          %p
            For any 2-monad
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi l
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_l
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_c
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_p
              (frequently written just
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                      %mi Alg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %li
              (if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is strict)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %msub
                      %mi Alg
                      %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_s
              of
              = succeed "-algebras" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p We have obvious 2-functors
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %msub
                            %mi Alg
                            %mi l
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↗
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %msub
                            %mi Alg
                            %mi s
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %msub
                            %mi Alg
                            %mi p
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ↘
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mi T
                          %msub
                            %mi Alg
                            %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{ &amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; T Alg_l \\
                  \&amp; &amp; &amp; \nearrow\\
                  T Alg_s &amp; \to &amp; T Alg_p\\
                  \&amp; &amp; &amp; \searrow\\
                  \&amp; &amp; &amp; &amp; T Alg_c }
          %p
            which are
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bijective+on+objects+functor"} bijective on objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/faithful+functor"} faithful
            on 1-cells, and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+fully+faithful+2-functor"} locally fully faithful
          %p
            Therefore, we can also assemble a number of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-categories"} F-categories
            of
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed "-morphism:" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            If we want to consider both lax and colax
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/double+category"} double category
            = succeed "-morphisms" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
          %p
            The 2-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_p
            is fairly well-behaved; for strict
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PIE-limits"} PIE-limits
            (if the base 2-category does), and therefore all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2-limits"} 2-limits
            (i.e. bilimits). When
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/accessible+functor"} accessible
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_p
            admits all 2-colimits as well (but not, in general, many strict 2-colimits).
          %p
            However, the 2-categories
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi l
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_l
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_c
            are not so well-behaved; they do not have many limits or colimits. But once we enhance them to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/F-categories"} F-categories
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rigged+limits"} rigged limits
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+morphism+classifiers"} weak morphism classifiers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mi s
                  %mo →
                  %mi T
                  %msub
                    %mi Alg
                    %mo *
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T Alg_s \to T Alg_*
            have left 2-adjoints.
